{{template "base.gohtml"}}

{{define "title"}}AuthThingie 2 Setup{{end}}

{{define "content"}}
    <div id="ftue-1-container" class="at-page">
        <hgroup>
            <h1>Welcome to AuthThingie 2</h1>
            <h2>Step 2 of 2 - From scratch or from AuthThingie 1?</h2>
        </hgroup>

        <p>
            Now that you have a config file and a database, we need to set up some users. If you have a previously working
            AuthThingie 1 installation, we can import your rules and your users from the config file you used. If you don't
            have a previous installation (or you want to start from scratch), you can do that as well.
        </p>

        <p id="ftue-choose-destiny">
            Choose your destiny&hellip;
        </p>

        <div id="ftue-destiny-buttons-container" class="grid at-card-grid">
            <article>
                <header>
                    <strong>First time here?</strong>
                </header>
                <p>
                    Create a brand new admin user and start with an empty set of rules. That user will be able to log in
                    right away and add everyone else later.
                </p>
                <footer>
                    <a href="/ftue/scratch">Start from scratch</a>
                </footer>
            </article>

            <article id="ftue-import-button-container">
                <header>
                    <strong>Upgrading from AuthThingie 1?</strong>
                </header>
                <p>
                    Bring your existing users and access rules across by handing me your old config file. Everything that
                    can be carried over will be, and you can tidy up the rest afterwards.
                </p>
                <footer>
                    <a href="/ftue/import">Import a config file from AuthThingie 1</a>
                </footer>
            </article>
        </div>

        <p class="at-footnote">
            This isn't your final configuration. Things can be changed after setup, of course.
        </p>
    </div>
{{end}}
